 ## Background
-The method originates from the need to jointly optimize camera poses and neural radiance fields [S3, unofficial]. The use of $se(3)$ Lie algebra for camera pose parameterization is a common technique in robotics [S3, unofficial]. The formulation addresses the ill-posed nature of shape-radiance ambiguity [S3, unofficial].
+The method originates from the need to jointly optimize camera poses and neural radiance fields [S3, unofficial]. The use of $se(3)$ Lie algebra for camera pose parameterization is a common technique in robotics [S3, unofficial]. The formulation addresses the ill-posed nature of shape-radiance ambiguity [S3, unofficial]. It is widely used in end-to-end training pipelines that rely solely on 2D re-rendering supervision without requiring explicit 3D ground truth [S4, unofficial].
 
